-gate","shared_router_encode_seconds":0.8960244009999769,"no_model_payload_bpb":0.02392578125,"no_model_route":"cheap-gate"},{"file":"random.txt","category":"random-64-symbol-alphabet","shared_router_payload_bpb":6.42578125,"shared_router_route":"neural-gate","shared_router_encode_seconds":3.342821908000019,"no_model_payload_bpb":6.4267578125,"no_model_route":"cheap-gate"}],"source_archives":{"large_sha256":"767f3e07004af0dee6dda14b9653609b621fad051e7a80367fcdc4514ec1fc29","artificial_sha256":"6d02ab02183a4cdbc39afb812b9fd038b44c97a2276b6d7afa79516ee69645f3"},"limits":["The primary probe/ratio policy was fixed before the Large Corpus holdout was evaluated.","Silesia is development/replication data because it was already used in PILOT-007.","Large Corpus results encode only the first 4096 bytes of each fixed file; full file size is reported separately.","The self-contained threshold accounts only for checkpoint bytes using the PILOT-007 observed gain, not CPU/energy cost.","The current POL1 shared-model container does not yet materialize a high-level model registry; experiments pass providers explicitly."],"run":{"github_actions_run_id":31941837032,"head_sha":"d0a45cb3e6e9438d5a09a493a32604ccc219cbd7","artifact_id":9262305581,"artifact_digest":"sha256:863d42926ffb0a34fff6273a89a06dd2d12eb3edeb6e4021007b56c3025a0b6f","benchmark_tests":"40 passed in 3.79s"},"post_run_verification":{"github_actions_run_id":31942331368,"head_sha":"b819981253a5835a790c9ea775fda3902cbc6e0c","tests":"41 passed in 3.87s","change":"Streams whose full length fits inside the probe are explicitly locked to the cheap route without evaluating the specialist.","benchmark_results_changed":false},"conclusions":["The two-stage routing mechanism is deterministic, lossless, and can stop specialist computation after locking the cheap route.","On the new fixed Large Corpus subset the shared router selected cheap for E.coli and neural for bible.txt and world192.txt, matching the qualitative value of the specialist on those prefixes.","The primary 256-byte probe with a 1:1 likelihood threshold is too permissive: it selected neural for all six Silesia development files and for the random64 control, including cases with negligible or negative neural value.","The probe itself has a measurable tax: on self-v2 the router is 2.1738 bpb versus the approximately 1.7095 bpb neural-gate reference because the first 256 bytes are forced through the cheap path.","When the model is unavailable, routing collapses exactly to the cheap universal path; under the self-contained checkpoint policy all three Large Corpus files stay cheap because their full sizes are below the 67.1 MB checkpoint-only break-even threshold.","PILOT-009 should refine activation confidence and probe length on already-consumed development data, then use a new holdout rather than retuning and re-claiming the Large Corpus as untouched."]}
